    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "body": "## Bug\n\nWhen a Claude Code Chat turn loses network access, Claude retries the API request with an attempt count and backoff delay. AO hides that state and continues to display only the generic Working timer.\n\n**Reported by:** subbu in Discord\n**Reported:** 2026-08-28\n**Analyzed against:** 5a51a3f90c4b649c21f92d1fcd58204e5e8e1a89\n**Confidence:** High \u2014 the exact Claude SDK event, ACP adapter behavior, daemon normalization boundary, and renderer fallback were traced and reproduced with deterministic protocol events.\n**Priority:** Medium \u2014 Chat remains usable after recovery, but users cannot distinguish productive work from a disconnected provider or understand retry timing.\n\n## Original report\n\n> I lost internet connection in my session. In vanilla Claude Code, if there is a network issue it shows API error and retry count and backoff time. In AO it just shows working.\n\n![AO remains on Working during a Claude connection failure](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Untrivial-ai/agent-orchestrator/issue-assets-claude-chat-retry-status/.issue-assets/claude-chat-retry-status/original-report.png)\n\n## Reproduction\n\n1. Start a Claude Code session in AO Chat mode.\n2. Send a prompt that reaches the Claude API.\n3. Disconnect the machine from the network while the turn is active.\n4. Observe the active turn status.\n\n## Expected\n\nAO shows the connection/API failure, retry attempt and maximum, and the next backoff duration, then clears the warning when output resumes.\n\n## Actual\n\nAO continues to display Working for ... with no indication that Claude is retrying.\n\n## Root cause\n\n- The bundled claude-agent-acp 0.64.2 adapter discarded api_retry SDK events.\n- The current adapter publishes retry failures only when the ACP client advertises the AIR sessionFailure extension.\n- The adapter omitted retry_delay_ms from that extension.\n- AO ignored session-info failure metadata, leaving the renderer with only the durable running-turn state and its generic Working fallback.\n\n## Fix\n\n[PR #4611](https://github.com/Untrivial-ai/agent-orchestrator/pull/4611) upgrades and patches the packaged adapter, negotiates the failure capability, normalizes failures into durable activities, renders them in the active turn, and settles the warning when provider output resumes.\n\n## Related\n\n- [PR #4216](https://github.com/Untrivial-ai/agent-orchestrator/pull/4216) \u2014 analogous transient transport-failure UX for Codex Chat.",
